WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
After the structural reduction, the full-rank branch has six candidates.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:15.000
These two coefficients belong to different factors. Their opposite signs do not cancel.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:24.000
For these semisimple rows, mixed terms vanish. Each coefficient tests its own simple factor.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:32.000
Opposite signs on different factors do not cancel: they are different tensor components.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:41.000
Five rows have no zero coefficient. Their radicals vanish.

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:49.000
In the final row, the E₆ coefficient is zero. The SU(3) coefficient is 27.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:57.000
E₆ is the radical. SU(3) remains a background global symmetry with a cubic anomaly.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:05.000
The representation is 27 tensor 3. Restricted to E₆, it becomes three copies of the 27.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:13.000
Along the paper’s Standard Model embedding, each 27 gives a family, a conjugate pair and two singlets.

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:18.000
Three net chiral Standard Model families, up to conjugation.
